      "evidence": "template/scripts/post_review_finalization.py (diff ~L580-582): detail = stderr + failing_lines(stdout), and the whole stdout is used only when detail is empty. If stderr holds only a generic lifecycle message and stdout has no recognisable failing line, stdout is dropped. The 'Archive failures report failing items' requirement and design decision 6 say the whole output is returned in that case.",
      "id": "finalization-failure-drops-unrecognised-stdout",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The spec says the whole output is reported when no failing-item line is recognisable. trusted_archiver does not do this whenever stderr is non-empty."
    },
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/openspec_lifecycle.py: FAILURE_LINE_RE = \u2717|\\[(?:ERROR|WARNING)\\]|\\berror\\b|\\bfailed\\b. The pattern is case-insensitive and also matches 'Totals: \u2026 1 failed' and any prose line containing 'error'. The extra matches can add noise, but they do not contradict the spec.",
      "id": "failure-regex-broader-than-design",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "FAILURE_LINE_RE keeps any line containing 'error' or 'failed' as a word. Design decision 6 lists only \u2717, [ERROR], [WARNING] and Error/error: lines."
